{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-explainer-about-snowboarding-write-like-you-are-talking-to-explain-clearly-common-words/audio/main-03f83b597d28.mp3","durationSec":176.784,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.88,"text":"Snowboarding is a recreational and competitive sport."},{"start":3.58,"end":7.06,"text":"A rider goes down a snow-covered surface while standing on a snowboard."},{"start":7.68,"end":10.44,"text":"The snowboard is the single board under the rider’s feet."},{"start":11.16,"end":12.52,"text":"Snowboarding is different from skiing."},{"start":13.16,"end":16.78,"text":"A skier uses two separate skis and usually faces forward."},{"start":17.46,"end":19.8,"text":"A snowboarder stands sideways on one board."},{"start":20.32,"end":21.78,"text":"Both feet are fixed to that board."},{"start":22.38,"end":26.12,"text":"One board and a sideways body position are important parts of snowboarding."},{"start":26.9,"end":30.14,"text":"Modern snowboarding equipment usually has three main things."},{"start":30.74,"end":33.72,"text":"These are a snowboard, special boots, and bindings."},{"start":34.6,"end":36.8,"text":"Bindings are the parts that lock the boots to the board."},{"start":37.62,"end":40.86,"text":"Snowboard bindings are not made to open automatically during a fall."},{"start":40.86,"end":42.6,"text":"Ski bindings can open."},{"start":43.46,"end":47.26,"text":"The locked snowboard is connected to a lower risk of knee injuries than skiing."},{"start":47.68,"end":51.66,"text":"On the source page, 15% of snowboard injuries are knee injuries."},{"start":52.18,"end":55.84,"text":"For skiing, 45% of all injuries are knee injuries."},{"start":56.6,"end":59.14,"text":"A snowboarder can put either foot first on the board."},{"start":59.78,"end":62.42,"text":"The word stance means the way the rider stands."},{"start":63.22,"end":65.88,"text":"In a regular stance, the left foot is first."},{"start":66.38,"end":68.92,"text":"In a goofy stance, the right foot is first."},{"start":69.7,"end":72,"text":"Both feet still stay fixed to the same snowboard."},{"start":72.48,"end":74.84,"text":"The difference is only which foot comes first."},{"start":75.62,"end":77.82,"text":"In both stances, the rider stands sideways."},{"start":78.54,"end":81.6,"text":"This is different from the usual forward-facing position in skiing."},{"start":82.96,"end":86.5,"text":"Snowboarding was first developed in the United States in 1965."},{"start":87.38,"end":91.12,"text":"In Muskegon, Michigan, Sherman Poppen fastened two skis together."},{"start":91.72,"end":92.76,"text":"He also added a rope."},{"start":93.42,"end":96.54,"text":"His wife, Nancy, named the snow toy the snurfer."},{"start":97.2,"end":100.88,"text":"The snurfer was an early snow toy made from two joined skis."},{"start":101.34,"end":102.16,"text":"It became popular."},{"start":102.64,"end":106.74,"text":"More than half a million snurfers were sold in 1966 alone."},{"start":107.24,"end":111.26,"text":"A manufacturer sold about one million of them during the next ten years."},{"start":111.88,"end":114.2,"text":"The sport continued to develop after the snurfer."},{"start":115.18,"end":120.74,"text":"In 1977, Jake Burton Carpenter started Burton Snowboards in Londonderry, Vermont."},{"start":121.54,"end":122.82,"text":"It was a company for snowboards."},{"start":123.82,"end":127.14,"text":"Snowboarding later became part of a large international sports event."},{"start":127.82,"end":130.68,"text":"It has been in the Winter Olympic Games since 1998."},{"start":131.72,"end":135.6,"text":"Today, it can still be recreational, which means people do it for enjoyment."},{"start":135.6,"end":140.14,"text":"It can also be competitive, with riders taking part in sports events."},{"start":141.22,"end":144.46,"text":"Niseko United is a real place for skiing and snowboarding in Japan."},{"start":145.26,"end":149.32,"text":"It has four resorts on one mountain, Niseko Annupuri."},{"start":149.32,"end":154.18,"text":"The mountain is 1,308 meters high and is 100 kilometers south of Sapporo."},{"start":154.86,"end":157.96,"text":"Its snow has a clear source, change, and result."},{"start":158.92,"end":160.96,"text":"Seasonal winds come from the Eurasian continent."},{"start":161.64,"end":164.78,"text":"They pick up moisture over warm currents in the Sea of Japan."},{"start":165.25,"end":167.04,"text":"This forms snow clouds."},{"start":168,"end":171.22,"text":"The resort page says the result is very dry, light powder."},{"start":171.22,"end":176.42,"text":"Riders of all abilities can use fresh powder or smooth, prepared runs there."}],"words":[{"text":"Snowboarding","start":0,"end":0.58},{"text":"is","start":0.58,"end":0.92},{"text":"a","start":0.92,"end":1.06},{"text":"recreational","start":1.06,"end":1.62},{"text":"and","start":1.62,"end":2},{"text":"competitive","start":2,"end":2.46},{"text":"sport","start":2.46,"end":2.88},{"text":"A","start":3.58,"end":3.72},{"text":"rider","start":3.72,"end":3.94},{"text":"goes","start":3.94,"end":4.2},{"text":"down","start":4.2,"end":4.48},{"text":"a","start":4.48,"end":4.68},{"text":"snow-covered","start":4.68,"end":5.26},{"text":"surface","start":5.26,"end":5.74},{"text":"while","start":5.74,"end":6.04},{"text":"standing","start":6.04,"end":6.38},{"text":"on","start":6.38,"end":6.56},{"text":"a","start":6.56,"end":6.7},{"text":"snowboard","start":6.7,"end":7.06},{"text":"The","start":7.68,"end":7.9},{"text":"snowboard","start":7.9,"end":8.38},{"text":"is","start":8.38,"end":8.56},{"text":"the","start":8.56,"end":8.74},{"text":"single","start":8.74,"end":9.06},{"text":"board","start":9.06,"end":9.38},{"text":"under","start":9.38,"end":9.74},{"text":"the","start":9.74,"end":9.9},{"text":"rider’s","start":9.9,"end":10.26},{"text":"feet","start":10.26,"end":10.44},{"text":"Snowboarding","start":11.16,"end":11.5},{"text":"is","start":11.5,"end":11.72},{"text":"different","start":11.72,"end":11.96},